{"kind":"assert","text":"Review note for Hugh: make review refusals explain the repair the author needs to make.\n\nRecommendation: distinguish a wrong primary at the reviewed head from a corrected head whose commitment still reports an older candidate. Use the existing review binding diagnostic and `gs review --prepare`. This is a small tooling improvement with high confidence in the problem and low implementation risk if it changes explanations only. It is advisory, awaiting your review; no implementation is assigned by this note.\n\nThe observed case is now complete. The worker correction at f0e3c40b was ready for its verdict, but the commitment still reported the live, approved cfd97a50 artifact at 870ee66f. The parent had the same publication problem. Planner's durable finding 4e5150cd identified three missing candidate retirements. Claude made those retirements; the same f0e head and review evidence then received approvals 04435544 and c650e07f. Receipt 2bf0b87b landed the head, closed both commitments, and main CI passed. The signed finding and approvals distinguish this from speculation about an idle service. No measured time saving is claimed.\n\nWhy the existing message confuses this case. [internal/reviewguard/binding.go](internal/reviewguard/binding.go@0fd9abd8829cbde06844c4c7dcb5507f3b3ab52c:375) tells the reviewer to name the commitment's current report first and keep the supplied artifact as a companion. That is useful for two artifacts at one head, which [internal/reviewguard/binding_test.go](internal/reviewguard/binding_test.go@0fd9abd8829cbde06844c4c7dcb5507f3b3ab52c:70) tests. Here the recommended report was at another head, so following that instruction could not review the intended correction. The reviewer correctly sought publication repair instead. The preference for a live approved report in [internal/workroom/fold.go](internal/workroom/fold.go@0fd9abd8829cbde06844c4c7dcb5507f3b3ab52c:3854) is deliberate; changing that policy is a larger question and is unnecessary for this fix.\n\nSmall remediation plan, based on main 0fd9abd8829cbde06844c4c7dcb5507f3b3ab52c:\n\n1. In missingPrimary, compare the supplied and currently reported artifacts' exact commit identities before suggesting reordering. Preserve the existing same-head guidance. For different heads, identify both records, heads, paths and the implementation request. Explain that the intended head is not currently the commitment's report and needs its author to inspect publication/succession. Where the durable facts establish the old-live-approved shape, state it precisely. Do not infer that every different-head artifact is a correction or prescribe unconditional retirement of another candidate.\n2. Keep the refusal and all binding, authority, artifact selection and fold rules unchanged. Do not substitute the older head, use evidence-only mode, or sign a retirement automatically. Explain how to inspect the named commitment and retry after its author repairs it. Preparation already exists: [docs/reference/gs/review.md](docs/reference/gs/review.md@0fd9abd8829cbde06844c4c7dcb5507f3b3ab52c:32). No new state, command or approval checkpoint is needed.\n3. Extend the resolver tests and the real command fixture in [cmd/gs/binding_test.go](cmd/gs/binding_test.go@0fd9abd8829cbde06844c4c7dcb5507f3b3ab52c:283). Prove that the same-head case still gives useful reordering advice, the different-head case gives the qualified publication explanation, preparation appends nothing, and author retirement of a replaced approved candidate lets the intended corrected head bind on the same commitment. An unrelated different-head companion must not receive an asserted correction/retirement instruction. Add a short troubleshooting example to the existing review page.\n\nExpected scope: binding.go, its tests, the CLI binding tests and the review page. Run the focused Go 1.26.7 tests (`go test ./internal/reviewguard ./cmd/gs -run 'TestResolve|TestPrepare' -count=1`) and the repository's required checks, followed by independent exact-head review and normal sealed delivery. If this requires a fold or authority change, return that finding for a separate decision. Source links above are pinned and previewable; the attached record summary supplies the before/after evidence. This review covers this observed diagnostic path, not a new whole-repository audit.","body":{"head":"0fd9abd8829cbde06844c4c7dcb5507f3b3ab52c","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0443554476d7ec04a2e95d50f2dbb3ec6bf89a42, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:2bf0b87b62989e44eb2f591797dfeca606c76a4d, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:4e5150cddc7e6379b9d41bbd3729231af6b3989d, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c650e07f587378c6ea3c919248bb9141e22e71fa stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:005460183c819676fead7d19fdd20633b48dc16c, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:015bb3acec403ed0d43bcd2a3c38bd188f7740ef, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0169ac61d80658478db25ce500d46d087c06fdde, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:02bae1e811fde13104ef614631ac608dca7a7295 and 212 more"}}